From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kai Krakow <kai@kaishome.de>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 02:31:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-drm: set the submit time of a flip only while it is
 queued

nv_drm_atomic_apply_modeset_config() enqueues each flip and writes its
submit time, its kick time and, for VRR flips, its raster frame after
that, right before applyModeSetConfig(), without holding flip_list_lock.
Once enqueued, the flip can be dequeued and freed by a flip event. Since
flip_list adds and completes at its head, that event can belong to an
earlier flip on the same crtc: with a nonblocking flip outstanding, a
blocking commit (VT switch, fbdev restore, a blocking modeset) enqueues
its flip without waiting, the outstanding flip's event dequeues the new
one and frees it, and the commit thread then writes into freed memory.
The kick time written after applyModeSetConfig() already goes through
nv_drm_crtc_set_flip_kick_time(), which checks under flip_list_lock that
the flip is still queued; the writes before it did not.

Do the same for the submit time: nv_drm_crtc_set_flip_submit_time()
looks the flip up under flip_list_lock and only then reads the raster
frame and writes the times. The times stay where they were, so the
bounds the flip events are reported with do not change.

Not reproduced; found by reading the code.

Fixes: 09660582deba ("nvidia-drm: fix vblank timestamp clock and flip event vblank")
Fixes: 6e1050732354 ("nvidia-drm: use the raster position register for vblank counts and VRR flips")
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.h    | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-modeset.c |  8 ++----
 2 files changed, 31 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.h b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.h
index 2d6008f5..a6f4291a 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.h
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.h
@@ -559,6 +559,35 @@ void nv_drm_crtc_raster_update_all(struct drm_device *dev);
 void nv_drm_crtc_set_flip_raster_frame(struct nv_drm_crtc *nv_crtc,
                                        struct nv_drm_flip *nv_flip);
 
+/**
+ * nv_drm_crtc_set_flip_submit_time - Set the submit time (and, for VRR
+ * flips, the raster frame) of a flip that is still in flip_list of crtc.
+ *
+ * Like nv_drm_crtc_set_flip_kick_time(): once enqueued, a flip can be
+ * dequeued and freed by a flip event at any time, also by the event of an
+ * earlier flip on the same crtc, since flip_list completes the newest
+ * entry first. Only touch it while it is still queued.
+ */
+static inline void nv_drm_crtc_set_flip_submit_time(struct nv_drm_crtc *nv_crtc,
+                                                    struct nv_drm_flip *nv_flip,
+                                                    NvU64 submit_time)
+{
+    struct nv_drm_flip *nv_queued_flip;
+
+    spin_lock(&nv_crtc->flip_list_lock);
+    list_for_each_entry(nv_queued_flip, &nv_crtc->flip_list, list_entry) {
+        if (nv_queued_flip == nv_flip) {
+            if (nv_flip->vrr) {
+                nv_drm_crtc_set_flip_raster_frame(nv_crtc, nv_flip);
+            }
+            WRITE_ONCE(nv_flip->kick_time, 0);
+            WRITE_ONCE(nv_flip->submit_time, submit_time);
+            break;
+        }
+    }
+    spin_unlock(&nv_crtc->flip_list_lock);
+}
+
 void nv_drm_enumerate_crtcs_and_planes(
     struct nv_drm_device *nv_dev,
     const struct NvKmsKapiDeviceResourcesInfo *pResInfo);
diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-modeset.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-modeset.c
index 9fec0716..37b229d7 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-modeset.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-modeset.c
@@ -605,12 +605,8 @@ nv_drm_atomic_apply_modeset_config(struct drm_device *dev,
         const NvU64 submit_time = ktime_get_ns();
 
         for (i = 0; i < num_submitted_flips; i++) {
-            if (submitted_flips[i]->vrr) {
-                nv_drm_crtc_set_flip_raster_frame(submitted_crtcs[i],
-                                                  submitted_flips[i]);
-            }
-            WRITE_ONCE(submitted_flips[i]->kick_time, 0);
-            WRITE_ONCE(submitted_flips[i]->submit_time, submit_time);
+            nv_drm_crtc_set_flip_submit_time(submitted_crtcs[i],
+                                             submitted_flips[i], submit_time);
         }
     }
 
